s="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKUBO, TADASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ZHANG, WENNONG</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAKU YASUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MURATA KENICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKUBO TADASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ZHANG WENNONG</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAKU, YASUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MURATA, KENICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKUBO, TADASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ZHANG, WENNONG</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>According to the prior art, a position controller has the problem that a low-frequency disturbance, and thus minute vibrations, may affect response because of the difficulty of adaptation to the phase of the vibrations. To solve the problem, there is provided a position controller, which comprises a subtractor (25) for subtracting a motor position signal from a movement position signal to produce an angle-of-twist signal; a high-pass filter (26) for advancing the phase of the angle-of-twist signal; a low-pass filter (27) for eliminating only high-frequency components of the signal received from the high-pass filter (26); a circuit (28) for multiplying the signal from the low-pass filter (27) by a torque-corrective gain to produce a torque-corrected signal; a torque correction evaluation section (29) for varying the torque-corrective gain according to a position deviation signal that is the difference between a position command and the movement position signal; and an adder (30) for combining the torque-corrective signal and the torque command to produce a new torque command.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Le problème des dispositifs de commande de position traditionnels est celui de la perturbation basse fréquence, et donc des vibrations régulières, qui peut notamment affecter la réponse, en raison de la difficulté d'adaption à la phase des vibrations. Pour résoudre ce problème, l'invention concerne un dispositif de commande de position comprenant : un soustracteur (25) destiné à soustraire un signal de position de moteur d'un signal de position de mouvement, afin de produire un signal d'angle de torsion; un filtre passe-haut (26) permettant d'avancer la phase de ce signal d'angle de torsion; un filtre passe-bas (27) destiné à éliminer uniquement les composantes haute fréquence du signal transmis par ledit filtre passe-haut (26); un circuit (28) conçu pour multiplier le signal du filtre passe-bas (27) par un gain de correction du débit, afin de produire un signal à débit corrigé; une section d'évaluation de correction du débit (29) permettant de faire varier ledit gain de correction du débit en fonction d'un signal de position de déviation représentant la différence entre une commande de position et le signal de position de mouvement; et un additionneur (30) destiné à combiner ledit signal de correction du débit et la commande débit, afin de produire une nouvelle commande débit.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest 